      ],
      "summary": "The desktop fits the applications that host it or join it. Hosting: `mountDesktop(node, { compact: { below } })` makes a narrow desktop compact, every window opening maximized and only the focused one shown; at any width the dock stays on screen, its tiles shrinking to fit and then scrolling, every module reachable by pointer and keyboard, and a keyboard user keeps their place when the dock redraws; `tray` decides the mail tile and the light/dark switch and adds a brand mark; `desktop.subscribe` reports every window change with its state, and when a module is `ready` or has `failed`; a shipped module learns from `visible` and `onVisibility` when its window is hidden; a host glyph is documented API. Framed applications: a framed module has `connectTimeoutMs` (15 s by default) to answer, past which its window says so, offers to try again and holds nothing open, and a module whose page reloads connects again on fresh ports. Joining: `connectToOs` takes `connectTimeoutMs` and `signal`, refuses with an `OsConnectError` (`OS0401`, `OS0403`) and leaves no listener behind, refuses a page that is not framed at once (`OS0402`), and keeps the application's own look with `presentation: \"none\"` or `{ root }`; `GrantedOperation` and `ToolBuilder` are exported. Windows open wholly on the desktop, keep their manifest's minimum size when resized, are labelled regions rather than dialogs, play their opening animation once and stop moving under reduced motion, and their glass survives a minified build. The assistant view opens, closes and toggles from the host, and builds its own Markdown only when the host renders none.",
      "id": "desktop-for-hosts"
    },
